{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792931759,"nonce":"GESXoNdZfGp4o8Wo/Jzs1jFH2ME=","title":"zylua: a generic for over string.gmatch allocates about seven heap objects per token","message":"tokenize is slower than PUC Lua 5.4 (CI Linux 272.9 ms vs 89.7, LuaJIT 38.1). Mac phases (zylua / PUC / LuaJIT): the gmatch loop 85 to 110 first run, 60 to 85 steady / 23 to 28 / 20 to 22 ms; counting with string keys 18 / 6.7 / 0.5. A string.find loop over the same pattern takes 31 ms against PUC's 26, so the matcher is near PUC and about half the gmatch time is the iterator protocol. Each run makes 6 collections and allocates 195 MB. Program-thread profile: the gmatch call subtree (zl_apply_2) 46%, zyntax_alloc 31% inclusive (15% self plus the thread-local lookup, collector 16%), host_pat_match_at 14%, string hashing and comparison 4 to 8%.\n\nPer token: `Lowerer::generic_for` (zyntax_lua/src/lower.rs) special-cases only pairs, ipairs and next, so the loop runs zl_call_2, then zl_values (a list header and storage around one result), then zl_value_at; `zl_gmatch_code` (library/patterns.rs) re-boxes env slots 4 and 5 with box_i64 on every match; zl_pat_captures builds an Any list; the capture string from zl_pat_cap_str is copied again by zb_box_str through $IO$string_to_dynamic, io_string_to_dynamic and string_copy (plugins/zrtl_io); zl_pack follows. Strings are not interned, so every counts[tok] rehashes and compares the bytes (cab506c covers interning, 1142d23 the per-allocation thread-local lookup).\n\nFix: lower `for ... in string.gmatch(s, p)` to a direct loop over zl_pat_match_at with typed position state and Str captures; box a fresh string by adopting it (io_string_adopt_dynamic) rather than copying; cache the hash in the string or intern short strings.","files":null}]}